<title>UK: Denmark sets $150 million two-year bond.</title>
<headline>Denmark sets $150 million two-year bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-08-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond was announced by joint lead managers Kankaku (Europe) Ltd and DKB International.</p>
<p> BORROWER   KINGDOM OF DENMARK</p>
<p> AMT    $150 MLN	COUPON     5.45 PCT  MATURITY    24.SEP.98</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  100.0     PAY DATE    24.SEP.96</p>
<p> FULL FEES  1.0	 REOFFER    =	   SPREAD	=</p>
<p> MOODY	AA1	 LISTING    UNLISTED  PAY FREQ    ANNUAL</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  AA+	 DENOMS (K) FIVE	SALE LIMITS =</p>
<p> NEG PLG    YES	 CRS DEFLT  =	   FORCE MAJ   IPMA (2)</p>
<p> GOV LAW    ENGLISH   HOME CTRY  =	   TAX PROVS   =</p>
<p> MGT/UND    0.15	SELL CONC  0.85	PRAECIP     =</p>
<p> NOTES	LAUNCHED OFF THE ISSUER'S PROGRAMME FOR THE ISSUANCE</p>
<p>		OF DEBT INSTRUMENTS</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
